1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,240
Short version, if you just got here.

2
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:07,040
I was three weeks behind on my rental car
when a passenger left two hundred grand in

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,440
my trunk. His daughter, Laura,
begged me to keep it safe.

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:15,760
Then a guy named Vince slid into my booth
at an all-night diner and offered me fifty

5
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,360
grand for it. I took the money.

6
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,600
I'm not proud of it, but
I promised you the truth.

7
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:25,093
Vince counted out fifty thousand
dollars in the diner parking lot,

8
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:28,160
in envelopes, like he'd
done it a hundred times.

9
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,520
Laura was still on the phone by her car.

10
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:32,880
She didn't see me hand him the bag.

11
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:34,320
Or maybe she did.

12
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:35,760
I never asked.

13
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:37,680
Vince didn't leave right away.

14
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:40,160
He set the duffel on the
hood of his gray sedan,

15
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:43,120
took out a pocketknife,
and cut open the lining.

16
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:46,240
That crooked stitching I'd
noticed at the gas station.

17
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:49,360
He reached inside and pulled
out a little thumb drive.

18
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,413
Then he held his phone to his ear.

19
00:00:51,467 --> 00:00:53,280
"Got it, boss," he said.

20
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,280
"The cash was just bait."

21
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:58,720
And he looked over at me and
smiled, like we were friends now.

22
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:00,360
Bait.

23
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:05,267
All that cash, and what they really
wanted was a tiny piece of plastic.

24
00:01:05,293 --> 00:01:07,920
And I'd just sold it for fifty grand.

25
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:10,560
On Monday morning, I caught up on the car.

26
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:13,640
By the end of the month, I'd
paid off the hospital too.

27
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:18,200
I wrote "paid in full" across that
bill and stuck it back on the fridge,

28
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:20,080
because I thought it would feel good.

29
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:21,200
It didn't.

30
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:24,480
Two weeks later, I saw
Harold on the local news.

31
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:28,380
Older guy, wrinkled suit,
walking into a courthouse.

32
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:31,667
"Accountant charged with
stealing from grocery chain."

33
00:01:31,693 --> 00:01:35,440
The money he supposedly stole
was the money from my car.

34
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:39,400
And whatever could have proved he
didn't was sitting in Vince's pocket.

35
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,840
Because of me.

36
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,800
I still drive.

37
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:46,120
I bought my own car eventually,
and it's all paid for.

38
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:50,027
Sometimes a passenger checks the
back window one too many times,

39
00:01:50,053 --> 00:01:53,560
and I think about Harold, leaning
forward from the back seat,

40
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,440
telling me he was sorry.

41
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,760
Months later, I got a text
from a number I didn't know.

42
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:00,107
It was Laura.

43
00:02:00,133 --> 00:02:02,213
"He's out on bail," she wrote.

44
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:03,720
"He's not angry at you.

45
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:06,640
He says he put you in an impossible spot."

46
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:09,240
I read that message about a hundred times.

47
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:14,240
At red lights, in line for coffee, at two
in the morning when I couldn't sleep.

48
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:17,547
I started typing back,
like, five different times,

49
00:02:17,573 --> 00:02:19,520
and deleted every one.

50
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:23,240
I think Harold was apologizing for
what he'd dropped on me that night.

51
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:27,000
He had no idea I'd be the
one who owed him an apology.

52
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:29,280
Some debts you pay off with money.

53
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:31,760
That one, I'm still paying.

54
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,200
That's ending one of four.

55
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:37,400
And trust me, there's a
lot you still don't know.

56
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:40,200
Like what Harold was
actually running from.

57
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,840
Go back and pick a
different path to find out.

58
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:45,080
The full map is pinned in the comments.
